CREATED-BY: VK3AVV VK Contest Log (Ver 4.15)
SOAPBOX: Operated mainly on 10m, but strayed onto 40m briefly Sat night
SOAPBOX: (VK2 time) to hand out zone 30. 10m condx weren't great on Sat
SOAPBOX: contest start saw only a few NA stations, and then more OC and AS
SOAPBOX: until one EU worked late afternoon, soon after 10m became very
SOAPBOX: noisy with no signals heard. Sunday was better: more NA stations
SOAPBOX: in the a.m., and many OC and AS stations during the day. Late
SOAPBOX: afternoon EU SP opened expected it to close shortly after sunset,
SOAPBOX: possibly followed by a late p.m. EU LP but SP stayed open for
SOAPBOX: hours with EU stations worked to 1500Z. Multipath evidenced by
SOAPBOX: echo-ey sigs, but not due to LP. Caribbean LP opened about 1230Z
SOAPBOX: with stations beaming EU worked, closing before 1600Z. Heard
SOAPBOX: northern SA stations answering EU CQs, but couldn't hear those
SOAPBOX: southern SA stations being worked by EU. Mon a.m. saw more NA
SOAPBOX: stations than Sat or Sun. An enjoyable contest given the onerous
SOAPBOX: starting condx. Thanks all who answered my calls, and thanks
SOAPBOX: managers for running this contest.
